1
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:12,932
June 13th,

2
00:00:12,982 --> 00:00:13,916
2026.

3
00:00:13,966 --> 00:00:18,609
One hour before Brazil's first
match at the World Cup,

4
00:00:18,659 --> 00:00:24,815
Zlatan Ibrahimović says this about Carlo
Ancelotti on American television.

5
00:00:24,865 --> 00:00:27,540
He means it as a compliment.

6
00:00:27,962 --> 00:00:29,811
Five months later,

7
00:00:29,861 --> 00:00:31,346
in Singapore,

8
00:00:31,396 --> 00:00:33,976
Japan beat Brazil three-two.

9
00:00:34,026 --> 00:00:35,802
In stoppage time.

10
00:00:35,852 --> 00:00:38,140
With Ancelotti sent off.

11
00:00:38,547 --> 00:00:43,117
It is the second time Japan have
beaten Brazil in thirteen months.

12
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:44,366
Before that,

13
00:00:44,416 --> 00:00:46,114
in fourteen matches,

14
00:00:46,164 --> 00:00:47,987
it had never happened.

15
00:00:48,037 --> 00:00:49,298
And suddenly,

16
00:00:49,348 --> 00:00:53,980
what Zlatan said that afternoon does
not sound like praise anymore.

17
00:00:59,010 --> 00:01:02,853
Brazil have not won the
World Cup since 2002.

18
00:01:02,903 --> 00:01:04,102
Yokohama.

19
00:01:04,152 --> 00:01:06,820
Ronaldo, Rivaldo, Ronaldinho.

20
00:01:07,232 --> 00:01:08,539
Since then:

21
00:01:08,589 --> 00:01:10,110
out to France.

22
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:12,324
Out to the Netherlands.

23
00:01:12,374 --> 00:01:14,752
Seven-one against Germany,

24
00:01:14,802 --> 00:01:15,895
at home.

25
00:01:15,945 --> 00:01:17,537
Out to Belgium.

26
00:01:17,587 --> 00:01:20,180
Out to Croatia, on penalties.

27
00:01:20,609 --> 00:01:22,765
For most of those years,

28
00:01:22,815 --> 00:01:24,695
Brazil had one plan.

29
00:01:24,745 --> 00:01:26,900
Give the ball to Neymar.

30
00:01:27,312 --> 00:01:28,731
So in 2025,

31
00:01:28,781 --> 00:01:34,377
Brazil hire the man who has managed
more stars than anyone alive.

32
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:36,233
Carlo Ancelotti.

33
00:01:36,283 --> 00:01:39,094
Five Champions League titles.

34
00:01:39,144 --> 00:01:40,564
And Zlatan,

35
00:01:40,614 --> 00:01:45,900
who played for him in Paris,
explains exactly how he does it.

36
00:02:01,407 --> 00:02:03,191
The studio laughs.

37
00:02:03,241 --> 00:02:05,730
That is what a manager does.

38
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:07,987
He keeps everyone happy.

39
00:02:08,037 --> 00:02:11,020
Zlatan finishes with one more line.

40
00:02:14,739 --> 00:02:17,634
There were signs before that.

41
00:02:17,684 --> 00:02:19,305
October 2025,

42
00:02:19,355 --> 00:02:20,420
Tokyo.

43
00:02:20,470 --> 00:02:24,161
Brazil lead Japan two-nil at half-time.

44
00:02:24,211 --> 00:02:26,389
They lose three-two.

45
00:02:26,439 --> 00:02:29,414
Japan's first win over Brazil,

46
00:02:29,464 --> 00:02:30,449
ever.

47
00:02:30,499 --> 00:02:33,553
It is Ancelotti's first defeat.

48
00:02:33,603 --> 00:02:36,180
It is called an accident.

49
00:02:36,609 --> 00:02:37,889
In May 2026,

50
00:02:37,939 --> 00:02:41,548
before he has coached a
single World Cup match,

51
00:02:41,598 --> 00:02:45,007
the federation extends his
contract to 2030.

52
00:02:45,057 --> 00:02:48,001
Nine and a half million euros a year.

53
00:02:48,051 --> 00:02:51,660
The best-paid national team
coach in the world.

54
00:02:52,091 --> 00:02:53,890
Seven weeks later,

55
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:55,811
at MetLife Stadium,

56
00:02:55,861 --> 00:02:58,373
Erling Haaland scores twice.

57
00:02:58,423 --> 00:02:59,725
Norway two,

58
00:02:59,775 --> 00:03:01,076
Brazil one.

59
00:03:01,126 --> 00:03:02,855
Round of sixteen.

60
00:03:02,905 --> 00:03:05,986
Brazil's worst World Cup since 1990.

61
00:03:06,036 --> 00:03:08,476
Neymar comes off the bench,

62
00:03:08,526 --> 00:03:11,820
scores a penalty, and it is not enough.

63
00:03:12,221 --> 00:03:13,279
And then,

64
00:03:13,329 --> 00:03:14,843
for a few weeks,

65
00:03:14,893 --> 00:03:16,277
it looks fine.

66
00:03:16,327 --> 00:03:18,818
Brazil beat Australia four-two.

67
00:03:18,868 --> 00:03:20,969
They beat India four-nil.

68
00:03:21,019 --> 00:03:24,879
The manager says he is happy
with the young players.

69
00:03:24,929 --> 00:03:27,420
That lasts until November 14th.

70
00:03:27,821 --> 00:03:29,185
Singapore.

71
00:03:29,235 --> 00:03:34,210
Raphinha wears the number ten and
the captain's armband.

72
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:35,780
Kubo scores.

73
00:03:35,830 --> 00:03:37,664
Nakamura scores.

74
00:03:37,714 --> 00:03:40,020
Japan two, Brazil nil.

75
00:03:40,444 --> 00:03:45,613
Then Vinícius hits one from outside
the box into the top corner.

76
00:03:45,663 --> 00:03:47,715
Then he scores again.

77
00:03:47,765 --> 00:03:48,874
Two-two.

78
00:03:48,924 --> 00:03:51,049
Endrick hits the post.

79
00:03:51,099 --> 00:03:52,934
Brazil are on top.

80
00:03:52,984 --> 00:03:57,500
This is the part of the story
where Brazil used to win.

81
00:03:57,931 --> 00:04:00,148
In the ninety-first minute,

82
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:03,128
João Gomes loses the ball in midfield.

83
00:04:03,178 --> 00:04:06,496
Brazil's players stop and
appeal for a foul.

84
00:04:06,546 --> 00:04:08,180
Japan do not stop.

85
00:04:08,611 --> 00:04:09,890
Three-two.

86
00:04:09,940 --> 00:04:12,105
Ancelotti is sent off.

87
00:04:12,155 --> 00:04:14,246
Raphinha is sent off.

88
00:04:14,296 --> 00:04:18,380
After the match, the manager
blames the referee.

89
00:04:18,812 --> 00:04:21,006
But look at what happened.

90
00:04:21,056 --> 00:04:24,703
Brazil's best player scored
two brilliant goals.

91
00:04:24,753 --> 00:04:27,277
And Brazil still lost to Japan.

92
00:04:27,327 --> 00:04:28,465
In Brazil,

93
00:04:28,515 --> 00:04:32,359
one newspaper writes that
after twenty-one matches,

94
00:04:32,409 --> 00:04:35,726
this team still has no
collective identity.

95
00:04:35,776 --> 00:04:38,762
That it depends on individual flashes.

96
00:04:38,812 --> 00:04:40,346
Read that again.

97
00:04:40,396 --> 00:04:42,260
Then go back to June.

98
00:04:59,995 --> 00:05:03,611
These are the numbers of
Ancelotti's Brazil.

99
00:05:03,661 --> 00:05:05,514
Twenty-one matches.

100
00:05:05,564 --> 00:05:06,995
Five defeats.

101
00:05:07,045 --> 00:05:09,039
Two of them to Japan.

102
00:05:09,089 --> 00:05:10,590
One World Cup,

103
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:14,749
and the country's worst finish
in thirty-six years.

104
00:05:14,799 --> 00:05:18,556
The best-paid coach in
international football.

105
00:05:18,606 --> 00:05:23,420
And after eighteen months, nobody
can say how his team plays.

106
00:05:23,831 --> 00:05:25,088
In Brazil,

107
00:05:25,138 --> 00:05:27,775
the reaction is not analysis.

108
00:05:27,825 --> 00:05:29,373
It is Romário.

109
00:05:29,423 --> 00:05:32,860
The man who won them the 1994 World Cup.

110
00:05:33,260 --> 00:05:38,159
The last World Cup came
twenty-four years after Yokohama.

111
00:05:38,209 --> 00:05:40,595
The next one is in 2030.

112
00:05:40,645 --> 00:05:42,194
Twenty-eight.

113
00:05:42,244 --> 00:05:47,980
And the contract Ancelotti signed in
May runs until the day it ends.

114
00:05:59,094 --> 00:06:04,342
Ancelotti says his team played the way
he wanted for seventy minutes.

115
00:06:04,392 --> 00:06:07,025
Zlatan was not criticising him.

116
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:12,185
He was describing the best manager of
stars the game has ever seen.

117
00:06:12,235 --> 00:06:15,625
But Brazil had twenty-four years of stars.

118
00:06:15,675 --> 00:06:19,959
What it never had was someone to
tell them how to move,

119
00:06:20,009 --> 00:06:21,335
where to go,

120
00:06:21,385 --> 00:06:22,986
and how to play.

121
00:06:23,036 --> 00:06:25,807
So did Brazil hire the wrong man?

122
00:06:25,857 --> 00:06:29,660
Or the right man for a
problem it does not have?
